docs/planning/decisions.md:2391:## D058 — UI v2 "Refined Native": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan
docs/planning/decisions.md:2451:## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8
docs/planning/decisions.md:2458:- The frozen prototype (D058, version 134) is the specification per screen; the
docs/planning/test-catalogue.md:44:- **T09 Native UI:** actual Tauri command path, menus/shortcuts, keyboard-only
docs/architecture/workflow-ledger.json:1053:      "dependency_contract": "per-UI-chunk T09 plus cumulative native quality",
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1111:        "check": "The cumulative T09 matrix: every earlier chunk's native acceptance (C01–C23) passes again on this bundle (their records under this chunk's evidence), covering menus, shortcuts, keyboard and focus, Accessibility roles and names, zoom, minimum window size, themes and reduced motion for every workflow."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1133:        "check": "T09 for the change review: keyboard only, Tab reaches the draft, Review again, Close, the confirmation field and Apply… in order and Shift-Tab returns in reverse; the focused control shows a visible accent focus ring; the impact text and every button carry accessible names; Escape on the native confirmation sheet cancels it and nothing is sent."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1189:        "check": "T09 matrix: every wizard step and the add sheet captured in light and dark at 100% and 200% zoom; Tab reaches each step's controls; at the 900×600 minimum the sheet's Cancel is inside the window once focused (the dialog scrolls within the viewport)."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1207:        "check": "The accessibility additions (DESIGN-V2 §8, T09) on the changed UI: from Read now, Tab reaches the Inbox tabs, the rows and the detail actions with every focused frame inside the window and Enter opens a row's detail; the read-status line is in the tree; the guard is the one topmost modal (the rail and page hidden beneath it, initial focus on Stay, the safe default, so Enter on arrival ends nothing) and Escape (Stay) returns focus to the switcher that asked; with macOS Reduce Motion on and the app relaunched a snooze toast persists past 8 s until dismissed (setting restored); at the 900×600 minimum and 200% zoom in both themes the Inbox columns stack so rows, the detail text and facts and every action stay inside the window with no horizontal scroll."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1261:        "check": "Keyboard and layout on both screens (T09): Test Cases' search and product filter in Tab order with the focus ring on a changed control; the API Client's Send reached by Tab from the URL and pressed with Space, its completion announced, with the focus ring on Send; the calls panel's control reachable with the ring and Space hiding the panel; Test Cases and the API Client at 900x600 and 200% in light and dark with no horizontal overflow."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1271:        "check": "The ported shell (R2App) with a tenant: the rail lists Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client and Administration with their ⌘ hints and the six products as Administration's children (the two gated ones tagged New), hidden and shown by the chevron; the status block shows Connected with the read status, Harness, Keychain and Jobs rows, and its Settings ⌘, button opens Settings; the 56px header shows the destination's title, the 260px 'Search or go to… ⌘K' button, the Explain switch (the show-the-calls preference: on shows the calls panel, off hides it) and Ask Harness, which opens the Harness; the rail's theme toggle switches the shown appearance between light and dark (D059 parity: the owner's approval of the composites is recorded in evidence/C35/parity/notes.md)."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1279:        "check": "Keyboard and layout (T09): Tab from the tenant button reaches the destinations, the status block, the header's search button, the Explain switch and Ask Harness in that order, with the focus ring on the search button; Space on the Explain switch flips the preference; Home, Inbox and Administration at 1440 wide by the display's full working height, and at 900×600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark with no horizontal overflow. Every row records the WebView's measured size from the accessibility tree and asserts it (1440 wide; exactly 900×600): a clamped resize never passes as the requested size."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1285:        "check": "Home as the prototype draws it (R2App start=home) with a tenant whose read has landed: the heading, the one-line read summary (products, the core's read status, the needs-action count) and Refresh; the Explain banner while the calls are shown and gone when they are not; six product cards in three columns, each naming its product, its pill (Connected, Partial, Needs a role, Connecting, Failed or Not available), a figure or an em dash with its metric, and a last line; the Runtime card's figure is the read's detection events and the Gateway card's its day's requests; the two gated products carry their gate and the New tag; opening a card opens that product in Administration; Needs attention lists the items needing action with their own action, Acknowledge and Snooze sending the core intents, or its empty state naming the read; Quick actions open the Playground, the Harness, the API Client and Academy (D059 parity: the owner's approval of the composites is recorded in evidence/C36/parity/notes.md)."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1289:        "check": "Keyboard and layout (T09): Tab from the heading reaches Refresh, each card, the attention row's controls and the quick actions in order, with the focus ring on a card; Enter on a card opens its product; Home at 1440 wide by the display's full working height and at 900×600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark, with no horizontal overflow; every row records the WebView's measured size from the accessibility tree and asserts it."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1295:        "check": "The Harness as the prototype board draws it (R2App start=harness) with a tenant, the Gateway workspace Team A chosen and its inference key stored, on the real pinned engine against the synthetic Gateway: the title band (heading; the tenant · engine · workspace line; End conversation beside the heading only while a conversation runs) over three columns; the rail labelled 'Saved conversations · encrypted' with New investigation and the live conversation's row; the transcript with the operator's message and the Harness's answer, and the composer whose Send is a button; the Decisions aside saying 'Nothing to decide yet' and listing the workspace's MCP catalog (both synthetic servers, each 'Not signed in') until a read-only desktop read waits, then holding that decision (airs_desktop.mcpServers, Read-only, Approve once / Decline) with the transcript's pending line; allowed in the aside the read is made once and the answer follows, the aside empty again. The parity composites (evidence/C38/parity, prototype left, app right at the WebView's measured size, light and dark) are captured from the state with the decision waiting; the owner's judgement is recorded in parity/notes.md before the gate (D059)."
docs/architecture/native-checks.json:1299:        "check": "Keyboard and layout (T09) with a decision waiting: Tab from End conversation reaches New investigation, the composer (Message) and its reachable action (Stop answering while the engine's turn waits on the decision, since Send is disabled until nothing is pending), then the aside's Approve once and Decline, in that order; the focus ring on that action; the Harness at 1440 wide by the display's working height and at 900×600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark, with the decision card populated, no horizontal overflow, New investigation, Send and Approve once each at least 32 CSS px, the rail, the composer and the aside side by side at 100% and one below the other at 200%; every row records the WebView's measured size and the viewport from its own tree and asserts them; the decision declined and the conversation ended leaves no engine."
